WHAT IS DERIVED
---------------

The probe catalogue in packages/engine/src/probes/catalogue.ts is derived from
the payload definitions in DiffingScan.java and TransformationScan.java of the
above work. The payload strings were extracted mechanically and decoded from
their Java string literals rather than reimplemented; they are substantially
the original author's work.

The scripts that performed that extraction are in docs/analysis/, along with
their output.

WHAT IS NOT DERIVED
-------------------

Everything else is an independent implementation. In particular the detection
engine, request layer, response featurisation, admission gate, throttling and
attribution logic were designed from the published research rather than ported
from the Java source, and share no code with it.

SIGNIFICANT CHANGES TO THE DERIVED PORTION
------------------------------------------

Required by section 4(b) of the Apache License. The following changes were made
to the extracted catalogue, each correcting a defect observed in the original:

1. The cheap "Basic function injection" gate that aborts the language cascade
   was moved from index 5 to index 0. In the original, Ruby, Python, JavaScript
   and shell were each fully probed before the gate that would have skipped
   them could fire.

2. corruptMagicValue was rewritten. The original wrote a filler character at
   index i modulo the value length for i in 0..3, which produced duplicate
   corruptions for values shorter than four characters and divided by zero on
   an empty value. An empty value is reachable from a trailing comma in a
   user-editable setting.

3. A duplicate ";" was removed from the transformation metacharacter list,
   which cost one wasted probe round per parameter.

4. The nginx alias-escape template no longer produces two identical escape
   payloads for single-character parameter values.

5. Each pair now declares whether its break and escape payloads can be made
   equal length, and by which strategy. 23 of 42 pairs and 11 of 14 language
   function triples had mismatched lengths in the original.

6. Payloads that are already in wire form, such as the parameter-pollution
   family, are marked as such so they are not percent-encoded a second time.

7. Probes whose semantics require the payload to be last in the value are
   marked end-anchored, because a trailing backslash is only an unterminated
   escape if nothing follows it.

The original catalogue, as extracted and before these changes, is preserved
verbatim in docs/analysis/probe_catalogue_raw.json so the divergence is
auditable.
